* An extremely [[productive]] suffix, it attaches to words or roots of [[Sino-Korean]] (e.g. {{m|ko|애국적|애국'''-적'''(愛國'''的''')|t=patriot'''ic'''}}) or Western origin (e.g. {{m|ko|[[쇼비니즘]]'''-적(的)'''|t=chauvinist'''ic'''}}) to form nouns (for whose usage see below).
* Except when directly [[attributive|attributing]] another word (where monolingual dictionaries usually classify this as a separate {{m|ko|관형사(冠形詞)|t=determiner}}), a noun formed using the suffix does not serve any function on its own and must either be used [[adnominal|adnominally]] / [[predicate|predicatively]] with {{m|ko|-이다|t=to [[be]]|pos=[[copula]]}} or [[adverbial|adverbially]] with {{m|ko|-으로|t=[[as]]; [[with]]|pos=[[instrumental]] case marker}}. See the following examples:
:: {{uxi|ko|애국'''-적''' 행동|t=A patriotic act {{q|attributive}}}}
:: {{uxi|ko|애국'''-적'''-인 행동|tr=aeguk'''-jeog'''-i-n haengdong|t=An act that is patriotic {{q|adnominal}}}}
:: {{uxi|ko|행동-이 애국'''-적'''-이다|t=The act is patriotic {{q|predicative}}}} 
:: {{uxi|ko|애국'''-적'''-으로 행동-하다|t=to act patriotically {{q|adverbial}}}}

