==Korean==

===Etymology 1===
{{anchor|yes}}
Not attested in Middle Korean. Probably from the same source as {{m|ko|네#yes|네}}, plausibly {{m|ko||*녜}} (not directly attested).

====Pronunciation====
{{ko-IPA|l=y}}

====Interjection====
{{ko-pos|interjection}}

# {{lb|ko|formal}} [[yes]] {{gloss|affirms the truth of the question as stated}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[한]] [[번]][[-은]] [[가]][[보다|-보셨습니까]]? — '''예''', [[가다|가]][[보다|-본]] [[적]] [[있다|있습니다]].|t=Have you been there at least once? — '''Yes''', I have been there.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[한]] [[번]][[-도]] [[가]][[보다|-본]] [[적]] [[없다|없습니까]]? — '''예''', [[없다|없습니다]].|t=Have you never been there? — No [lit. '''Yes'''], never.}}
#* {{quote-book|ko|year=late 19th c.|title=ko:열여춘향슈졀가 上|trans-title={{w|Chunhyangjeon|Song of the Virtuous Girl Chunhyang Preserving her Chastity}}|text=^통인[[아]] '''예''' [[저|져]] [[건너|건네]] [[화류]] [[중|즁]][[에|-의]] [[오락가락]] [[희뜩희뜩|힛ᄯᅳᆨ힛ᄯᅳᆨ]] [[얼른|얼는]][[얼른|얼는]] [[하|ᄒᆞ는]] [[거|겨]] [[무엇|무어]][[이다|신지]] [[자세히|자셔이]] [[보다|보와라]]|t="Hey, Tong-in!" "'''Yes, sir.'''" "Go look carefully at what that thing over there, amid the flowers and willows, might be: the thing that is hurrying back and forth in flashes of white."|subst=ᄯᅳᆨ//뜩,ᄒᆞ//하}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Korean has a number of words for "yes". {{m-self|ko|예}} is highly polite and formal (appropriate in an interview), {{m|ko|네}} is polite but less formal (appropriate in a conversation with parents), and {{m|ko|응}} and {{m|ko|어}} are  plain and non-formal (appropriate in a conversation with friends).
* As in the example above, Korean "yes" follows the [[polarity]] of the question, unlike in English. Hence saying "yes" to a negatively stated question means that the negative is true.

