===Etymology 1===
{{ko-etym-native|gy|寶妲|*pòtól|dot=,}}<ref name="Lee90" /> probably a compound of an ancient root for "daughter" {{IPAfont|*pòt-}} + suffix {{IPAfont|*-ól}}; compare ''Jilin leishi'' {{okm-l|丫妲|*àtól|3=son}}, apparently equivalent to {{IPAfont|*à(N)t-}} + {{IPAfont|*-ól}}.<ref>{{cite-journal|year=2002|title={{lang|ko|「{{ruby|[鷄](계)[林](림)[類](유)[事](사)」}}의 여성 명칭어 연구}}|trans-title=Study on terms for women in the ''Jilin leishi''|journal=Asia yeoseong yeon'gu|volume=41|pages=243—268}}</ref>

{{ko-etym-native|yb|ᄯᆞᆯ〮|stól|hangul=y}} The {{IPAfont|*/p-/ > /s-/}} shift is difficult to explain; perhaps it simply "represents an irregular development", or perhaps the expected cluster {{IPAfont|*/pt-/}} had already fully merged and was realized in speech only as {{IPAfont|[t͈-]}}, which was misanalyzed as the surface realization of the cluster {{IPAfont|/st-/}}.<ref name="Lee90">{{cite-book|last=Lee|first=Ki-Moon|last2=Ramsey|first2=S. Robert|title=A History of the Korean Language|publisher=Cambridge University Press|year=2011|isbn=978-0-521-66189-8|page=147}}</ref> 

Choi Yeong-Seon believes that the character {{m|mul|寶}} in {{m|mul|寶}}{{m|mul|妲}} is a corrupted spelling of {{m|mul|實}} (Late Middle Chinese {{IPAfont|*/ʑiɪt̚/}}), and that the true Late Old Korean lexeme should be {{IPAfont|*sùtól}} or a similar form. If this is true, the Middle Korean reflex {{l|okm|ᄯᆞᆯ〮}} would be entirely regular, requiring only the elision of a minimal vowel.<ref>{{cite-thesis|year=2015|author={{lang|ko|최영선}} (Choi Yeong-Seon)|title={{lang|ko|계림유사의 음운론적 연구}}|trans-title=A phonological study on the ''Jilin leishi''|publisher=Chonnam National University|url=https://scienceon.kisti.re.kr/srch/selectPORSrchArticle.do?cn=DIKO0013736847}}</ref>

