===Etymology 2===
{{anchor|training}}
{{ko-etym-native|ws|질〮|cíl}}

Was subject to hypercorrection by Seoul speakers to avoid the {{IPAfont|/ki/ > /t͡ɕi/}} palatalization in southern dialects, producing {{inh|ko|ko-ear|길|tr=kil}}; {{m|ko|김치}} and {{m|ko|기와}} are two other well-known examples of this phenomenon. Non-standard dialects commonly preserve the original form.

====Pronunciation====
{{ko-IPA|a=y}}

====Noun====
{{ko-noun}}

# {{lb|ko|of animals}} [[training]]; [[domestication]]
#: {{ux|ko|[[그]] [[개]][[-는]] '''길'''[[-이]] [[잘]] [[들다|들어서]] [[말]][[-을]] [[잘]] [[듣다|듣는다]].|The dog is obedient because it was well-'''trained'''.|lit=The dog is obedient because '''training''' has well entered it.}}
# {{lb|ko|of tools, etc.}} [[break in|breaking in]]; [[wear]]
#: {{ux|ko|[[갓]] [[사다|산]] [[새#new|새]] [[신발]][[-이라]] [[아직]] '''길'''[[-이]] [[안]] [[들다|들었다]].|Having just bought these shoes, they haven't been broken in yet.|lit=Having just bought these shoes, '''breaking in''' hasn't entered them yet.}}
