===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|ss|것|kès|dot=,}} from {{inh|ko|oko|物叱|tr=*KAs}}.

The now colloquially dominant contraction {{ko-l|거}} is first attested in the nineteenth century.

===Pronunciation===
{{ko-IPA|a=Ko-것.oga}}
* {{ko-tone|H}}

===Dependent noun===
{{ko-pos|dependent}}{{cln|ko|lemmas|nouns}}

# [[thing]]; [[something]]; [[that]] [[which]]; [[what]]; {{n-g|used to designate any object, action, or phenomenon, forming noun phrases.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[이]] [[중]][[-에서]] [[제일]] [[크다|큰]] '''게''' [[뭐]]야?|What's the biggest '''one''' out of these?|audio=이 중에서 제일 큰 게 뭐야.ogg}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[이]] [[곳]][[-에]][[-는]] [[바위]] [[같다|같은]] '''것'''[[-이]] [[정말]] [[많다|많습니다]].|Here, there are very many '''things''' that look like rocks.|audio=이 곳에는 바위 같은 것이 정말 많습니다.ogg}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[적군]][[-이]] ^[[서울]][[-에]] [[진입]][[하다|한]] '''것'''[[-으로]] [[판단]][[되다|됩니다]].|We judge that the enemy has entered Seoul.|lit=We judge it as the '''thing''' that the enemy has entered Seoul.|audio=적군이 서울에 진입한 것으로 판단됩니다.ogg}}
#: {{syn|ko|바|pos1=for abstract nouns, formal}}
# an object belonging to an owner; {{non-gloss|forms constructions equivalent to English possessive pronouns. Colloquially pronounced {{ko-inline|꺼}} with initial tensing.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[이]] [[세상]][[-은]] [[우리]][[-들]][[-의]] '''것'''[[-이다|-이었지만]], [[이제]][[-는]] [[너희]][[-들]][[-의]] [[것]][[-이다]].|This world was ours, but now it’s yours.|audio=이 세상은 우리들의 것이었지만, 이제는 너희들의 것이다.ogg}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[이]] [[연필]] [[친구]] '''건'''[[데]]?|But this pencil is my friend''''s'''.|audio=이 연필 친구 건데.ogg}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[저]] [[집]][[-도]] [[우리]] '''거'''[[-야]].|That house is '''ours''', too.|audio=저 집도 우리 거야.ogg}}
# {{q|after the suffix {{m|ko|-ㄴ}}}} {{non-gloss|Emphasizes the speaker's certainty about the preceding verb or adjective.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[인생]][[-은]] [[원래]] [[헤어지다|헤어지는]] '''거'''[[-야]].|Life is always about saying goodbye.|lit=Life is always a '''thing''' where you say goodbye.|audio=인생은 원래 헤어지는 거야.ogg}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[걔]][[-는]] [[태어나다|태어날]] [[때]][[-부터]] [[그런]] '''거'''[[-야]].|He must have been like that since he was born.|lit=He is a '''thing''' like that since he was born.|audio=걔는 태어날 때부터 그런 거야.ogg}}
# {{non-gloss|Used as an element in a number of verbal suffixes; see the "Derived terms" section.}}

====Usage notes====
As a dependent noun, {{m|ko||것}} and its colloquial variant cannot occur in isolation, but must always be attributed by a verb, an adjective, a determiner, or a possessor.

In colloquial Korean, {{m|ko|거}} is the generally accepted form of this important dependent noun, to the point that the use of the uncontracted form may feel awkward and artificial. In formal language, {{m|ko||것}} remains preferred.

In the colloquial language, {{m|ko||거}} changes somewhat based on noun case, which is unusual for Korean:

* The nominative form is almost always {{m|ko||게}}, instead of the expected {{m|ko|[[거]][[가]]}}
* The instrumental form is generally {{m|ko|걸로}} rather than the expected {{m|ko|[[거]][[로]]}}, although the latter form is also  common
* As mentioned, the possessed form is always {{m|ko|꺼}}.

See also the very common short forms {{m|ko|건}} instead of {{m|ko|[[거]][[는]]}} and {{ko-inline|걸}} instead of {{m|ko|[[거]][[를]]}}, although the full forms are also widely found.

