===Etymology 1===
{{ko-etym-native|ss|그|kù}}

The 3rd-person pronoun sense is widely believed to be introduced together with {{m|ko|그녀}} by {{w|Kim Dong-in}} in the early 20th century,<ref>Chae-un {{smallcaps|Yi}} ({{lang|ko|이재운}}), ''Ttŭt to morŭgo chaju ssŭnŭn uri mal ŏwŏn 500-kaji'' ({{lang|ko|뜻도 모르고 자주 쓰는 우리말 어원 500가지}}), 2008, {{ISBN|978-89-5913-339-0}}</ref> probably calque of {{der|ko|ja|-}} {{ja-r|彼|かれ}}, which became a personal pronoun in addition to a demonstrative pronoun due to the influence of European languages.
However, the demonstratives {{m|okm|이〮}}, {{m|okm|그}}, and {{m|okm|뎌〮}} were all used occasionally in Middle Korean as 3rd person pronouns as well.<ref>{{cite-journal|year=2015|author=ko:박재희|pages=103-128|title=ko:3인칭대명사 ‘그’에 관한 소고|volume=71|journal={{lang|ko|한민족어문학}}}}</ref>

