{{ko-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ko-etym-native|yb|어리〮다〮|èlí-tá}} Originally meant only "to be foolish"; the "to be young" sense developed in the sixteenth century, because children are foolish and immature, and eventually became the main sense of the word. It partly displaced the original word for "to be young", {{m|ko|젊다}}, which now specifically means "to be youthful", i.e. people in their teens and twenties. The "to be foolish" sense was largely replaced by {{m|ko|어리석다}}, originally a derived term.

====Adjective====
{{ko-adj}}

# to be [[young]], to be [[little]], to be a [[child]]; {{n-g|when used for people, usually younger than mid-teens unless used in a comparison}}
#: {{uxi|ko|[[내]] '''어린''' [[시절]]|t=my childhood}}
#: {{ux|ko|'''어릴''' [[때]][[-에]][[-는]] [[누구]][[-나]] [[순수하다]].|t=Everyone is innocent when they are '''young'''.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[나]][[-는]] [[열]][[일곱|-일곱]] [[살]][[-이다|-이니]] [[언니]][[-보다]] [[세]] [[살]] '''어리다'''.|t=Since I am seventeen, I am three years '''younger''' than my sister.}}
# to be [[naïve]]; to be [[immature]]
#: {{ux|ko|[[대학생]][[-은데|-인데]] [[너무]] [[생각]][[-이]] '''어리다'''.|t=They're university students, but they think too '''naively.'''}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[행동]][[-을]] [[보다|보니]] [[아직]] [[어리다]].|t=Looking at his behavior, he is still '''childish'''.}}
# {{lb|ko|humble}} to be [[ignorant]]; to be [[foolish]]
#: {{syn|ko|어리석다}}
#: {{uxi|ko|[[제]] '''어린''' [[생각]]|t=my '''humble''' opinion}}

