{{ko-etym-native|ss|아ᄒᆡ〮|àhóy|dot=,}} from earlier {{inh|ko|oko|阿孩|tr=*ahoy}}. While the word is native, the second syllable was identified already in the 8th-century ''hyangga'' poem ''Anmin-ga'' with {{cog|ltc|孩|t=child}}. Historically, the word was often mistakenly perceived as Sino-Korean, with the spelling {{m|ko|兒孩}}, a [[phono-semantic matching]]. See {{m|ko|아해}}.

