=====Usage notes=====
{{sense|guy; person}}
* As {{m|ko|애|t=guy; person}} is extremely colloquial, {{m-self|ko|아이}} is sometimes used to replace it in less colloquial writing, especially in the pronominal forms {{m|ko|걔}}, {{m|ko|얘}}, {{m|ko|쟤}}. This is less common in speech.
* Such a replacement is even rarer when {{m|ko|애}} is being used non-pronominally, because {{m-self|ko|아이}} is perceived as being neither sufficiently colloquial as {{m|ko|애}} nor sufficiently non-colloquial as e.g. {{m|ko|사람}}. It is very normal, if highly colloquial, to refer to American people in general as {{m|ko|[[미국]] '''애'''[[-들]]}}, but {{m|ko|[[미국]] '''아이'''[[-들]]}} will usually refer specifically to American children.

