김치:
==Korean==
{{wp|ko:}}
[[File:Korean Gimchi01.jpg|thumb|{{m-self|ko|김치}}]]

===Etymology===
Ultimately composed within Korea of {{der|ko|zh|-}}-derived morphemes {{ltc-l|沉|submerged, soaked}} and {{ltc-l|菜|vegetable}}, i.e. "fermented vegetable". {{ko-etym-native|hm|nocat=y|딤ᄎᆡ|timchoy}}

In most dialects, Middle Korean {{okm-inline|딤ᄎᆡ|timchoy}} was regularly [[palatalize]]d to {{m|ko|짐츼}}, whence modern southern dialectal {{m|ko|짐치}}. However, southern Korean dialects also palatalized {{IPAfont|/ki/}} to {{IPAfont|/t͡ɕi/}}, which the Seoul prestige dialect did not. Seoul speakers hence [[hypercorrect]]ed {{m|ko|짐츼}} to {{m|ko|김츼}} to avoid sounding "southern", whence modern Standard {{m|ko|김치}}.

This word displaced the older {{noncog|okm|-}} term {{okm-l|디히〮|tìhí}} (whence {{ko-l|지}}, now only used in compound words and the southern Gyeongsang and southwestern Jeolla dialects), probably because regular sound change rendered it monosyllabic and caused it to have a large number of homophones.

===Pronunciation===
