===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|bs|고〯맙다〮|dot=,}} attested only in conjugated forms.

The word is almost certainly a contraction of {{m|okm||*고〯마〮ᄒᆞᆸ다〮}}, the regularly derived {{m|ko|—[[브]]}} adjective from the verb {{okm-inline|고〯마〮ᄒᆞ다〮|kwŏmáhòtá|3=to respect; to admire}}. In Middle Korean, {{m|okm||고〯맙다〮}} had the meaning of "to be worth respecting; to be worth admiring", as would be expected from regular {{m|okm||-브-}} adjectives. The source verb was displaced by Sino-Korean loans in the Early Modern period, when the derived adjective's semantic shift to "to be thankful" also occurred.

===Pronunciation===
{{ko-IPA|l=y}}

===Adjective===
{{ko-adj|irreg=y}}

# (to be) [[thankful]]
#: {{syn|ko|감사하다<qq:more formal>}}
