# to [[form]]; to [[shape]]; to [[occur]]
#: {{uxi|ko|나무 아래에 그늘이 '''졌다'''.|Shade has formed under the tree.}}
# {{lb|ko|auxiliary|after the {{m|ko|-어|tr=-}}/ {{m|ko|-아|tr=-}} infinitive}} to [[become]], to [[get]]: {{n-g|turns adjectives into processive verbs; expresses change in state.}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|새롭다||alt2=새로워지다|t1=to be [[new]]|t2=to become [[new]]}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|용감하다||alt2=용감해지다|t1=to be [[brave]]|t2=to become [[brave]]}}
# {{lb|ko|auxiliary|after the {{m|ko|-어|tr=-}}/ {{m|ko|-아|tr=-}} infinitive}} {{n-g|forms intransitive or passive verbs from processive verbs; see usage notes.}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|지나가다||alt2=지나가지다|t1=to [[pass]], [[go]] [[through]]|t2=to be possible to [[pass]], [[go]] [[through]]}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|막다||alt2=막아지다|t1=to [[block]]|t2=to be [[block]]ed}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|주다|주어지다|t1=to [[give]]|t2=to be [[given]]}}
# {{senseid|ko|intransitive-passive}} {{lb|ko|auxiliary|after the {{m|ko|-어|tr=-}}/ {{m|ko|-아|tr=-}} infinitive|unproductive}} {{n-g|suffix which formed intransitive passive constructions; usually the constructions have deviated from the original modern meaning of the verbs.}}
#: {{cot|ko|-뜨리다}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|부수다|부서지다|t1=to [[break]]|t2=to be [[shatter]]ed}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|떨다|떨어지다|t1=to [[tremble]]|t2=to [[fall]]}}

=====Usage notes=====
* For the ''second'' auxiliary sense, the meaning of the suffix differs if the verb is intransitive, intransitive passive, or transitive.
** For intransitive verbs, the suffix usually adds the meaning of potentiality, which, usually, goes over the speaker's expectations of the action happening.
** For intransitive passive verbs, the suffix doesn't add any special meaning. This is usually done when the base transitive verb cannot take {{m|ko||-어지다}}: {{m|ko|읽다}} -> {{m|ko|읽혀지다}}, but {{m|ko||*읽어지다}} is not correct. However, do note that this use of {{m-self|ko||-어지다}} is seen to be incorrect by [[w:National Institute of Korean Language|the National Institute of Korean Language]].
** For transitive and ditransitive verbs, the suffix forms an intransitive verb with passive meaning. In such case, not every verb can have {{m|ko||-어지다}} added to it; see above.

