====Usage notes====
* The verbal stem usually took the form {{m|okm|잇다|잇-|tr=is-}} before a consonant-initial suffix, and {{m|okm|이시다|이시-|tr=isi-}} before a vowel-initial one.
* In the seventeenth century, the semantic gap widened so that the former eventually morphed into the modern past tense marker {{m|ko|-었-}}, while the latter form survived as an auxiliary. Thus Modern Korean has the [[doublet]] {{m|ko|[[사람]][[-이]] [[죽다|죽]][[-었-]][[-다]]|t=a person died}} and {{m|ko|[[사람]][[-이]] [[죽다|죽]][[-어]] [[있다]]|t=a person is there, [lying] dead}}, both coming from the same Middle Korean verb.

