{{ko-etym-native|''Gwonyyeom yorok'' ({{lang|ko|勸念要錄 / 권념요록}})|므슨|musun|1637|hangul=y|dot=,}} probably a [[hypercorrection]] of {{inh|ko|okm|-}} {{okm-inline|므슴〮|mùsúm}} that was motivated by the adnominal suffix {{m|ko|-은}} common in determiners.

Variants of {{okm-inline|므슴〮|mùsúm}} with final {{m|ko||ㅁ}}, e.g. {{m|ko|무슴}} and {{m|ko|무삼}}, remained more common than {{lang|ko|므슨}} or {{lang|ko|무슨}} until the mid-nineteenth century and are still used by some older speakers of {{w|Gyeongsang}} dialect.

