===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|wi|그ᅀᅳ다〮|kùzù-tá|dot=,}} from pre-MK {{IPAfont|*kùsùk-}}, a form preserved in many dialects; compare {{cog|ko-jeo|끄슥다}}, {{cog|ko-gys|끄시다}}, {{cog|ko-yuk|끄스다}}.

The modern Standard Korean form is highly irregular, involving not only spontaneous initial tensing (a common if irregular process in Korean) but an inexplicable addition of {{IPAfont|/l/}}; the expected reflex is {{m|ko||*그다}} or {{m|ko||*끄다}}. The same irregular shift occurred somewhat earlier in {{m|ko|이끌다|t=to lead}}, which probably affected this verb's development.

===Pronunciation===
{{ko-IPA|l=y}}

===Verb===
{{ko-verb-set|끌다|끌리다|끌리다}}
{{ko-verb}} {{tlb|ko|transitive}}

# to [[pull]], to [[draw]], to [[drag]]
#: {{uxi|ko|[[의자]][[-를]] '''끌다'''|t=to '''drag''' a chair}}
#: {{uxi|ko|[[수레]][[-를]] '''끌다'''|t=to '''pull''' a wagon}}
#: {{uxi|ko|[[저수지]] [[물]][[-을]] '''끌어'''[[오다]]|t=to '''draw''' water from a reservoir}}
#: {{uxi|ko|[[자전거]][[-를]] '''끌다'''|t=to '''drag''' a bicycle}}
# {{lb|ko|of people, animals}} to [[lead]], to [[drag]]
#: {{uxi|ko|[[애]][[-들]][[-을]] '''끌고''' [[병원]][[-에]] [[가다]]|t=to '''drag''' the kids to the hospital}}
# {{lb|ko|with no object}} to [[drag on]]
#: {{uxi|ko|[[영화]][[-가]] [[질질]] '''끈다'''|t=the movie '''drags on''' tediously}}
# to [[stall]], to [[delay]]
#: {{uxi|ko|[[시간]][[-을]] '''끌다'''|t=to '''stall''' for time}}
# {{lb|ko|figurative}} to [[draw]], to [[attract]]
#: {{uxi|ko|[[관광객]][[-을]] '''끌다'''|t=to '''draw''' tourists}}
#: {{uxi|ko|[[관심]][[-을]] '''끌다'''|t=to '''draw''' attention}}
# {{lb|ko|figurative}} to [[draw]] {{gloss|inspiration, sourcing, etc., from}}

