==Korean==

===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|gci|착ᄒᆞ다|chak-hota|dot=,}} combining adjective-forming {{okm-l|ᄒᆞ다|hota}}, with [[cranberry morpheme]] {{m|ko||착}}. Equivalent to modern {{af|ko|착|-하다|t2=to do|pos2=[[light verb]] deriving adjectives}}.

Other than this unusually early attestation, the word only reappears after c. 1700. The original manuscript of the ''Gyechuk ilgi'' is lost and the versions that currently survive may have been subject to edits to the manuscript several decades to more than a century later, and Kim Yang-jin 2015 argues that this word is actually a late seventeenth-century loan-calque from {{bor|ko|mnc|ᠴᠠᡴ ᠰᡝᡵᡝ |t=to be strict, to be orderly}}, with {{m|mnc|ᠰᡝᡵᡝ}} being translated to its Korean equivalent {{m|ko|하다}}.

Alternatively, perhaps derived from the [[ideophone]] {{ko-l|착|calmly, calmingly, tiredly}}, or the homophonous ideophone {{ko-l|착|sticking tight}}.

