==Korean==

===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|ss|거ᇧ다〮|kèsk-tá}} The initial consonant underwent spontaneous gemination in the eighteenth century, a phenomenon recurrent in the Modern stage of Korean and motivated by sound-symbolic effects.

The Old Korean ancestor is attested in the infinitive form as {{m|oko||折叱可|tr=*KEska}} in the ''Heonhwa-ga'', an eighth-century ''hyangga'' poem. While the nature of Old Korean orthography—where only the final phonemes of the verb stem are shown—makes an exact phonological transcription of this inflected verb impossible, the form demonstrates that the Old Korean word for "to snap" (equivalent to {{noncog|zh|折}}) also ended in *-sk or *-skV.

===Pronunciation===
{{ko-IPA}}

===Verb===
