=====Usage notes=====
* The particle is attached to {{m|ko|-에|t=at}}, {{m|ko|-에게|t=to}}, {{m|ko|-한테|t=to}}, and {{m|ko|-으로|t=with, by}}, and with certain adverbs or nouns referring to place, direction, or means. Historically, it could also combine with {{m|ko|-을|pos=accusative case marker}}, but this is now fully obsolete.<ref name="Jeon" />

===Etymology 2===
{{ko-etym-native|''Cheoyong-ga'' ({{lang|ko|處容歌 / 처용가}})|如可|*-taka|4=1281}} The ''Cheoyong-ga'' is claimed to be from the ninth century but is almost certainly of much later provenance, possibly as late as the thirteenth century. Not attested in earlier Old Korean sources.

{{ko-etym-native|ss|-다가〮|-tàká|hangul=y}}

Further etymology unclear. In 13th century ''{{w|gugyeol}}'' texts, this suffix appears as {{m|okm|-入舍可|tr=*-tosyaka}} when fused with the honorific suffix {{m|okm|-으시-}}. This suggests that it is a compound of {{okm-l|-더〮-|-té-|5=imperfect past suffix}} + {{okm-l|-오〮-|-wó-|5=unclear suffix, perhaps the modulator}} + {{okm-l|-가〮|-ká|5=unclear suffix}}.<ref>{{cite-journal|author=ko:박진호|journal=ko:국어의 시대별 변천 연구 3|title=ko:고대 국어 문법|year=1998|publisher=ko:국립국어연구원}}</ref>

However this is incompatible with the tonal pattern, as the syllable {{lang|ko|다}} has low pitch rather than the high pitch expected from this etymology. Perhaps the pitch was affected by that of the particle, although Kim Seong-gyu rejects this possibility.<ref>{{cite-journal|author={{lang|ko|김성규}} (Kim Seong-gyu)|journal=Gugyeol yeon'gu|title=ko:성조에 의한 어미의 분류 - 중세국어를 중심으로 -|trans-title=Classification of suffixes according to tone: Centering on Middle Korean|volume=27|year=2010|pages=243—295}}</ref>

