#* {{quote-book|ko|year=2003|month=March|author=ko:신지영|publisher=ko:한국문화사|isbn=8957260145|title=ko:우리말 소리의체계: 국어음운론 연구의 기초를 위하여|trans-title=The Sound System of Korean Language: For the Fundamentals of Korean phonology Research|text=[[우리말]][[-의]] [[경우]][[-는]] [[언어학]][[적]] [[의미]][[-를]] [[가지다|가진]] [[모든]] [[소리]][[-들]][[-이]] [[하나]][[-도]] [[예외]] [[없다|없이]] [[폐]][[-에서]] [[내뿜다|내뿜는]] [[기류]][[-를]] [[이용하다|이용하여]] [[만들어지다|만들어지는]] '''부아''' [[날숨]] [[소리]][[-이다]].|translation=In the case of Korean, all sounds with linguistic meanings are, without exception, '''pulmonic''' egressive sounds, made by utilising airflow coming out from the lungs.}}
#* {{quote-web|1=ko|date=15 October 2020|author=Kwon O-gil|work=ko:[생물이야기] 폐의 건강 진단해주는 '폐활량'<1150>|trans-work=[Biological Story] Lung capacity, which diagnoses the health of the lungs.|url=http://www.kwnews.co.kr/nview.asp?aid=220101400010|text=[[물론]] [[운동]][[-을]] [[하다|하는]] [[사람]][[-의]] [[폐활량]][[-이]] [[보통]] [[사람]][[보다]] [[많다|많고]], 25[[세]][[-에]] [[가장]] [[폐활량]][[-이]] [[제일]] [[크다|크다가]] [[점점]] [[줄어들다|줄어들어]] 60[[세]] [[정도]][[-에]] 20~30% [[감소하다|감소하고]], [[늙다|늙을]][[수록]] [[점점]] [[줄다|준다]]. [[이렇게]] '''부아'''[[-도]] [[늙다|늙는다]].|t=Of course, the lung capacity of the person who exercises is higher than that of the average person; lung capacity is the largest at the age of 25, and it then gradually decreases as a person ages, with 20-30% of lung capacity lost when one reaches 60 years of age. Like this, the '''lungs''' get old.|title=Archived copy|accessdate=21 October 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20201024143355/http://www.kwnews.co.kr/nview.asp?aid=220101400010|archivedate=24 October 2020}}
