===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|dy|몽이|mwongi}} Attested somewhat later in the eighteenth century as {{m|ko|모이}}. From reconstructed {{inh|ko|okm|-}} {{okm-inline|*모ᅀᅵ〮|*mwòzí}}, from pre-Middle Korean {{IPAfont|*mwòsí}}. The majority of modern dialects still preserve the ancestral form {{m|ko|모시}}.

While not directly attested in Middle Korean, the Middle Korean verb {{okm-inline|모ᅀᅵ〮다〮|mwòzí-tá|3=to graze cattle}} is clearly related. The ancestral word appears to have meant "feed; fodder" in general, not specific either to cattle or poultry. The semantics narrowed to "feed for poultry" in most modern dialects, but to "cattle" in Middle Korean and also in the modern {{w|Yukjin dialect}}, where {{m|ko||모시}} means "fodder for cattle".<ref>{{cite-journal|author=ko:박경래, 곽충구, 이기갑, 강영봉|title=ko:새로 발굴한 방언(9)|trans-title=Newly discovered dialectal forms (9)|journal=Bang'eonhak|year=2012|volume=15|pages=287—338}}</ref>

