==Korean==
{{wp|ko:}}

===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|bdb|거믄〮고〮|kèmún-kwó}}. 

Two theories exist on the origin of the word, first is based on its Sinitic synonym [[현금]]([[玄琴]]), which can be translated as "black zither" thus making 거문고 a word composed of two roots: [[검은]] and *고, morpheme otherwise non-attested anywhere except [[가얏고]], a native synonym to  other musical instrument, more widely known as gayageum ([[가야금]]), so *고 part is accepted as native gloss for [[琴]].

Altaic theory, in its turn, proposes a connection, derivation or borrowing, with both [[komuz]], from Turkic sphere, and Manchu [[ᡴᡠᠮᡠᠨ]].

