-음:
{{also|음}}

==Korean==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ko|-ㅁ}} {{q|after vowel-final and {{m|ko|ㄹ}}-final verbal stems}}

===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|dot=,}} from {{inh|ko|okm|-}} {{okm-l|-음〮|-úm}}, {{okm-l|-ᄋᆞᆷ〮|-óm}}.

This suffix is the most common Middle Korean nominalizer, including in the ''[[gugyeol]]'' sources of the fourteenth century and in the Hangul sources of the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries, but is very rarely attested in pre-fourteenth-century [[Old Korean]] sources. Choe 2017 comments that no intermediary stage appears to exist, and that this sudden post-fourteenth-century dominance of an apparently novel grammatical suffix is puzzling and difficult to explain.

The older nominalizers were [[realis]] {{m|okm|隱|tr=*-n}} and irrealis {{m|okm|尸|tr=*-l}}, both of which are now [[adnominal]] suffixes.

In Middle Korean, {{okm-l|-음〮|-úm}} proper only derived nouns from verbs, while verbal substantives ("-ing", "that...") were formed by bimorphemic {{okm-l|-움〮|-wú-m}}, the first element traditionally being analyzed as the "modulator" suffix {{okm-l|-우〮-|-wú-}}. The "modulator" disappeared around the late sixteenth century, leaving {{m-self|ko|-음}} to do double duty.

===Suffix===
{{ko-pos|suffix}}

# [[-ness]]; [[-tion]]; [[-ment]] {{q|noun-deriving suffix for verbs and adjectives}}
#: {{syn|ko|-기}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|[[나누다|나누]]-|t1=to divide|나눔|t2=divi'''sion''', charity}}
#: {{suffixusex|ko|[[기쁘다|기쁘]]-|t1=happy|기쁨|t2=happi'''ness'''}}
# {{lb|ko|formal}} the [[act]] of, the [[process]] of, [[-ing]], [[being]]{{...}}, to [[be]]{{...}} {{q|[[gerund]]- or [[noun]] [[clause]]-forming suffix for verbs and adjectives}}
#: {{syn|ko|-기|pos=non-formal}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[우리]][[-가]] [[만나다|만'''남''']][[-은]] [[우연]][[-이]] [[아니다]].|Our meet'''ing''' [each other] cannot be an accident.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[이]][[-가]] [[옳다|옳]][[-지]] [[않다|않]]'''음'''[[-은]] [[명백하다|명백-한]] [[사실]][[이다|-입니다]].|This not be'''ing''' right is an evident fact.}}
# {{lb|ko|formal|or|Internet|slang}} {{n-g|A formality-neutral sentence ender used in certain contexts when one desires to avoid formality distinctions, such as in formal reports or Internet conversations.}}
#: {{usex|ko|[[생물학]][[-에]] [[크다|큰]] [[관심]][[-을]] [[가지다|가지고]] [[있다|있'''음''']].|[Student] has great interest in biology.|footer=(in a school report)}}
#: {{usex|ko|2020[[년|-년]] 12[[월|-월]] 9[[일|-일]][[-에]] '''[[쓰다|씀]]'''.|Written on 9 December, 2020.|footer=(in the preface of a book)}}
#: {{usex|ko|[[님]], [[거기]] '''[[가다|가]] [[보다|봄]]'''?|Have you been there?|footer=(in an Internet conversation)}}

====Usage notes====
* In non-formal language, {{m|ko|-기}} is used instead to turn verbs and adjectives into substantives.
* This suffix has an [[epenthetical]] vowel and therefore provokes verbal irregularities in certain stems, e.g. {{m|ko|그립다|그립-|t=to long for}} > {{m|ko|그리움|t=longing}}.
* This suffix does not elide preceding {{m|ko|ㄹ}}; instead, the epenthetical vowel is lost, e.g. {{m|ko|살다|살-|t=to live}} > {{m|ko|삶|t=life}}.

