====Usage notes====
* Korean does not grammatically distinguish between singular and plural nouns. Thus, while {{m|ko|사람들}} means "people", {{m|ko|사람}} can mean either "person" or "people", depending on context.
* {{m-self|ko|들}} has a nuance of emphasizing the individuality of each item. Compare the following:
*: {{ux|ko|[[아이]][[-가]] [[공부]][[-만]] [[하다|해서]][[-는]] [[안]] [[되다|된다]].|t=Children [a child in a generic sense; children as a collective group] should not just be studying.}}
*: {{ux|ko|[[아이]]'''들'''[[-이]] [[공부]][[-만]] [[하다|해서]][[-는]] [[안]] [[되다|된다]].|t=The children [specific children, or simply emphasizing the individuality of children] should not just be studying.}}
*: {{ux|ko|[[우리]][[-가]] [[하다|하는]] [[말]] [[좀]] [[듣다|들어]][[보다|봐]].|t=Listen for a bit to what we are saying.}}
*: {{ux|ko|[[우리]]'''들'''[[-이]] [[하다|하는]] [[말]] [[좀]] [[듣다|들어]][[보다|봐]].|t=Listen for a bit to what we [each of us] are saying.}}
* {{m-self|ko|들}} is not typically used for a quantified noun, except in a construction where the classifier precedes the quantified noun and is linked by the genitive particle {{m|ko|의}}.
*: {{uxi|ko|[[두]] [[사람]]|t=two people}}
*:: {{uxi|ko|[[두]] [[사람]]'''들'''|t=two people (but uncommon)}}
*: {{uxi|ko|[[사람]] [[두]] [[명]]|t=two people}}
*:: {{uxi|ko|[[사람]]'''들''' [[두]] [[명]]|t=two out of some larger group of people}}
*: {{uxi|ko|[[두]] [[명]][[-의]] [[사람]]|t=two people}}
*:: {{uxi|ko|[[두]] [[명]][[-의]] [[사람]]'''들'''|t=two people}}
* {{m-self|ko|들}} is obligatory after the deictic determiners {{m|ko|이|t=this}}, {{m|ko|그|t=that}}, {{m|ko|저|t=that}}.
*: {{uxi|ko|[[저]] [[사람]]|t=that person}}
*: {{uxi|ko|[[저]] [[사람]]'''들'''|t=those people}}
* {{m-self|ko|들}} can be used after an adverb or an object to pluralize the subject, especially when the subject has been omitted.
*: {{uxi|ko|[[빨리]]'''들''' [[먹다|먹어라]]|t=quick, let's eat|q=command to a group of people}}
*: {{uxi|ko|[[밥]]'''들''' [[먹다|먹어라]]|t=let's eat rice|q=command to a group of people}}

