===Etymology===
{{ko-etym-native|ss|-어〮셔〮|-é-syé|dot=,}} from {{inh|ko|okm|-}} {{okm-l|-어〮|-é|5=infinitive suffix}} + {{okm-l|-셔〮|-syé|5=location postposition}}. The postposition is from the infinitive of the verb {{okm-l|이시다〮|ìsìtá|3=to be at}}.

It was uncommon in the fifteenth century but increasingly became more widespread.<ref>{{cite-journal|title=ko:[원인]을 나타내는 연결어미에 대한 통시적 고찰 — <노걸대언해>류를 중심으로 —|author=ko:안주호|year=2002|journal=Eoneohak|volume=34|pages=133—158|trans-title=On the historical development of purposive connectives in Korean: Focusing on the ''Nogeoldae eonhae''}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{ko-IPA}}

===Suffix===
{{ko-yin form of|-아서}}
{{ko-pos|suffix}}

# [[because]], [[since]]: {{n-g|a suffix used to express that the first clause is the cause or reason to the second clause.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[미안]], [[아기]][[-가]] [[시끄럽다|시끄러워'''서''']] [[잘]] [[안]] [[들리다|들려]]...|Sorry, I can't hear you well '''because''' my kid's being noisy.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[많이]] [[먹다|먹'''어서''']] [[배]][[-가]] [[아프다|아파졌다]].|I got a stomachache '''because''' I ate too much.}}
# [[by]] [[-ing]], [[while]] [[-ing]]: {{n-g|a suffix used to specify the manner or means of the following clause.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[빗자루]][[-를]] [[쓰다|써'''서''']] [[청소]][[-를]] [[하다|하자]].|Let's clean '''by''' us'''ing''' the broom.}}
#: {{ux|ko|미연[[-아]], [[눕다|누워'''서''']] [[밥]][[-을]] [[먹다|먹지]] [[말다|마라]]!|Miyeon, don't eat '''while''' lying '''down'''!}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[서다|서'''서''']] [[먹다|먹으면]] [[건강]][[-에]] [[안]] [[좋다]].|If you eat '''while''' stand'''ing''', it is not good for your health.}}
# [[and]] [[then]], [[and]]: {{n-g|a suffix used to indicate that two or more connected actions happen in a sequential order; the first clause usually establishes the state, position, location, or the object of the second clause.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[철수]][[-는]] [[도서관]][[-에]] [[가다|가'''서''']] [[공부]][[-를]] [[시작하다|시작했어요]].|Cheolsu went to the library '''and then''' started studying (''at the library'').}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[라면]][[-을]] [[끓이다|끓여'''서''']] [[먹다|먹었어]].|I made ramyeon '''and then''' ate it.}}
#: {{ux|ko|[[공원]][[-에서]] [[친구]][[-를]] [[만나다|만나'''서''']] [[영화]][[-를]] [[보다|보]][[-러]] [[가다|갔다]].|I met up with my friend at the park '''and then''' went to watch a movie (''with them'').}}

====Usage notes====
* For vowel harmony, contractions, and allomorphy, see {{m|ko|-어#Usage_notes|-아/어/여}}.
* {{m|ko|-어서}} cannot be used with the tense markers {{m|ko|-겠-}} and {{m|ko|-었-}} in the standard language, but this is still found in colloquial speech.
* When in the sense of ''so'', ''since'', {{m|ko|-어서}} cannot be followed by [[w:Imperative mood|imperative]] or [[w:Propositive mood|propositive]] clauses.
* The words {{m|ko|반갑다}}, {{m|ko|감사하다}}, {{m|ko|고맙다}}, {{m|ko|좋다}}, {{m|ko|죄송하다}}, and {{m|ko|미안하다}} commonly follow the {{m|ko|-어서}} clause.

